lifeos-nix patch f4-d — privacy: Atlas asset-graph makes no egress, and the tab stays off

PROBLEM
  Atlas (LIFEOS/ATLAS/) maintains a SQLite graph of the entire estate: Cloudflare
  workers/domains/DNS, repos, projects, machines, devices, scanner targets, and
  credential-class assets. Secret VALUES never enter the graph (upstream anti-claim A1
  holds — verified), but the SHAPE of the estate is itself sensitive: what is owned,
  what depends on what, which domains lack auth-boundary coverage, which credentials
  exist and at which vendor. Upstream's own doc calls it "a map of the estate — hence
  local-only, outside git, behind FDE".

  The CLI honours that: `atlas owns|blast|exposed|stale|unregistered|sql|export|insights`
  is read-only local SQL with ZERO Inference calls (grep over Atlas.ts + Store.ts + all 8
  collectors = 0). But PULSE/modules/atlas.ts:96 spawned `TOOLS/Inference.ts` over the
  full metrics JSON to write the Insights narrative, cached to
  MEMORY/STATE/atlas-insights.json and refreshed fire-and-forget on any graph change.
  That is one automated egress path carrying a structural map of everything owned.

  Upstream ships `atlas = true` in base PULSE.toml, so on a machine where the tick unit
  IS installed the narrative generates on its own.

KILLED HERE (two layers, deliberately redundant)
  1. modules/atlas.ts — `inference()` HARD KILL: the Bun.spawn of Inference.ts is removed
     entirely and the function returns null with one log line. No flag can re-enable it;
     the derivation itself is privacy-hard (same reasoning as f4-b elevenlabs). The
     Insights panel degrades to metrics-only — deterministic local SQL, zero egress —
     and every other Atlas route (snapshot, browse, gaps) is unaffected.
  2. PULSE.toml [modules] — `atlas = false` (whole surface off; pulse.ts:311 then never
     imports the module) plus a new `atlas_insights = false` marker documenting that the
     narrative is off at the code layer too. Belt and braces, on Klemen's explicit call.

DELIBERATELY NOT TOUCHED
  - The Atlas CLI, Store, collectors, and systemd templates: all local, all useful, no
    egress. Nothing here blocks running `atlas` by hand.
  - metrics() — spawns `atlas insights`, i.e. local read-only SQL, not a model.

RELATED, STILL OPEN (see the gradbišče PASTI.md #13)
  Nothing calls InstallAtlas.ts — not the upstream installer, not this flake — so no tick
  unit, no DB, and Pulse /atlas 404s even with the flag on. That accidental gap is what
  kept the estate off the wire so far. A bug is not a security control: this patch is the
  decision written down, so the day the installer is wired (upstream or here) the graph
  still makes no egress. Wiring the timer into the nix module is separate future work.

DECISION PROVENANCE
  Klemen, 2026-08-31: "Atlas se mi zdi brutalno nevaren za data leak Anthropicu, morda bi
  morala s tem počakat da sva local … dajva kar Atlas false in počaka, oz. lahko je in
  atlas_insights na false, in še atlas false. tako, da je res temeljito dokler nisva local
  in se ga lotiva." Also his: lucky that upstream has not wired the installer yet, since
  our defense must live in our fork rather than depend on their gap.

VERIFICATION
  Post-build: `grep -c 'Bun.spawn' modules/atlas.ts` = 1 (the local `atlas insights` CLI
  call, NOT Inference); `grep -n 'atlas' PULSE.toml` shows atlas=false + atlas_insights=false.
  Hunks generated by `git diff` against pristine 7.40.4 with f4-c and f-derived-watch-config
  already applied (never hand-counted).

